1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:09,260
Chapter 30 The more I knew of the inmates of more house, the better I liked them.

2
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:13,703
In a few days I had so far recovered my health

3
00:00:13,705 --> 00:00:17,099
that I could sit up all day and walk out sometimes.

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:22,919
I could join with Diana and Mary in all their occupations, converse with them as

5
00:00:22,921 --> 00:00:27,199
much as they wished, and aid them when and where they would allow me.

6
00:00:27,959 --> 00:00:31,858
There was a reviving pleasure in this intercourse,

7
00:00:31,858 --> 00:00:34,720
of a kind now tasted by me for the first time.

8
00:00:35,599 --> 00:00:42,601
The pleasure arising from perfect congeniality of tastes, sentiments and principles.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,519
I like to read what they like to read, what they enjoyed, delighted me,

10
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,160
what they approved, I reverenced.

11
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,819
They loved their sequestered home.

12
00:00:53,779 --> 00:00:59,660
I too, in the grey small antique structure, with its low roof, its lattice

13
00:00:59,661 --> 00:01:05,163
casements, its maulering walls, its avenue of aged furs,

14
00:01:05,163 --> 00:01:08,400
all grown a slant under the stress of mountain winds.

15
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:13,158
It's garden, dark with you and holly, and where no

16
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:16,160
flowers but of the hardiest species would bloom.

17
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,000
Found a charm both potent and permanent.

18
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:27,000
They clung to the purple moors behind and around their dwelling, to the hollow veil

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,324
into which the pebbly bridlepath leading for their gate

20
00:01:31,326 --> 00:01:35,379
descended, and which wound between fern banks first.

21
00:01:36,419 --> 00:01:41,120
And then amongst a few of the wildest little pasture fields that ever bordered a

22
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:46,160
wilderness of heath, or gave sustenance to a flock of gray moorland sheep,

23
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,260
with their little mossy-faced lambs.

24
00:01:49,739 --> 00:01:54,779
They clung to this scene, I say, with a perfect enthusiasm of attachment.

25
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:59,900
I could comprehend the feeling, and share both its strength and truth.

26
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:03,300
I saw the fascination of the locality.

27
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,599
I felt the consecration of its loneliness.

28
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:13,680
My eye feasted on the outline of swell and sweep, on the wild coloring communicated

29
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:17,974
to ridge and del by moss, by heathbell, by flower-sprinkled

30
00:02:17,976 --> 00:02:22,080
turf, by brilliant bracken and mellow granite crag.

31
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:27,158
These details were just to me what they were to

32
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:30,620
them, so many pure and sweet sources of pleasure.

33
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:36,239
The strong blast and the soft breeze, the rough and the halcyon day,

34
00:02:36,959 --> 00:02:41,839
the hours of sunrise and sunset, the moonlight and the clouded night,

35
00:02:42,519 --> 00:02:46,099
developed for me in these regions, the same attraction as for them,

36
00:02:47,099 --> 00:02:51,000
wound round my faculties, the same spell that entranced theirs.

37
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,660
In doors we agreed equally well.

38
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:58,620
They were both more accomplished and better read than I was.

39
00:02:59,459 --> 00:03:04,500
But with eagerness, I followed in the path of knowledge they had trodden before me.

40
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:07,360
I devoured the books they lent me.

41
00:03:08,419 --> 00:03:11,296
Then it was full satisfaction to discuss with them

42
00:03:11,298 --> 00:03:14,180
in the evening what I had perused during the day.

43
00:03:15,059 --> 00:03:19,059
Thought fitted thought, opinion met opinion.

44
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:22,400
We coincided in short perfectly.

45
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:27,239
If in our trio there was a superior and a leader, it was Diana.

46
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:32,239
Physically she far excelled me, she was handsome, she was vigorous.

47
00:03:33,339 --> 00:03:37,800
In her animal spirits there was an affluence of life and certainty of flow,

48
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:42,459
such as excited my wonder, while it baffled my comprehension.

49
00:03:43,519 --> 00:03:46,716
I could talk a while when the evening commenced,

50
00:03:46,716 --> 00:03:50,300
but the first gush of vivacity and fluency gone.

51
00:03:51,239 --> 00:03:55,980
I was feigned to sit on a stool at Diana's feet, to rest my head on her knee,

52
00:03:56,660 --> 00:04:01,076
and listen alternately to her and Mary, while they

53
00:04:01,076 --> 00:04:04,639
sounded thoroughly the topic on which I had but touched.

54
00:04:05,459 --> 00:04:07,919
Diana offered to teach me German.

55
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,360
I liked to learn of her.

56
00:04:11,139 --> 00:04:14,400
I saw the part of instructor is pleased and suited her.

57
00:04:15,099 --> 00:04:18,059
That of scholar pleased and suited me no less.

58
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:25,779
Our nature's dovetailed, mutual affection of the strongest kind was the result.

59
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:28,059
They discovered I could draw.

60
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:31,940
Their pencils and color boxes were immediately at my service.

61
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:38,300
My skill, greater in this one point than theirs, surprised and charmed them.

62
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,680
Mary would sit and watch me by the hour together.

63
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:48,959
Then she would take lessons and a docile, intelligent, assiduous pupil she made.

64
00:04:50,059 --> 00:04:57,120
Thus occupied, and mutually entertained, days passed like hours and weeks like days.

65
00:04:57,919 --> 00:05:02,167
As to Mr. Sinjin, the intimacy which had arisen so naturally

66
00:05:02,167 --> 00:05:06,440
and rapidly between me and his sisters did not extend to him.

67
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:10,667
One reason of the distance yet observed between

68
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:14,239
us was that he was comparatively seldom at home.

69
00:05:15,379 --> 00:05:20,860
A large proportion of his time appeared devoted to visiting the sick and poor

70
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,959
among the scattered population of his parish.

71
00:05:25,379 --> 00:05:29,300
No weather seemed to hinder him in these pastoral excursions.

72
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:34,519
Rain or fair, he would, when his hours of morning study were over.

73
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,300
Take his hat.

74
00:05:36,699 --> 00:05:39,779
And followed by his father's old pointer,

75
00:05:39,781 --> 00:05:44,180
Carlo, go out on his mission of love or duty.

76
00:05:44,459 --> 00:05:46,819
I scarcely know in which light he regarded it.

77
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:52,800
Sometimes, when the day was very unfavorable, his sisters would expostulate.

78
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:58,800
He would then say with a peculiar smile, more solemn than cheerful.

79
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:04,339
And if I let a gust of wind or a sprinkling of rain turn me aside from

80
00:06:04,341 --> 00:06:07,684
these easy tasks, what preparation would such

81
00:06:07,684 --> 00:06:11,661
sloth be for the future I propose to myself?

82
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:17,002
Diana and Mary's general answer to this question was a

83
00:06:17,002 --> 00:06:20,360
sigh, and some minutes of apparently mournful meditation.

84
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:28,000
But besides his frequent absences, there was another barrier to friendship with him.

85
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:33,959
He seemed of a reserved, and abstracted, and even of a brooding nature.

86
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:39,879
Zealous in his ministerial labours, blameless in his life and habits,

87
00:06:40,519 --> 00:06:45,739
he yet did not appear to enjoy that mental serenity, that inward content,

88
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:51,919
which should be the reward of every sincere Christian and practical philanthropist.

89
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:58,319
Often, of an evening, when he sat at the window his desk and papers before him,

90
00:06:59,059 --> 00:07:04,639
he would cease reading or writing, rest his chin on his hand, and deliver

91
00:07:04,641 --> 00:07:10,699
himself up, to I know not what course of thought, but that it was perturbed and

92
00:07:10,701 --> 00:07:16,519
exciting might be seen in the frequent flash and changeful dilation of his eye.

93
00:07:17,139 --> 00:07:20,107
I think more over, that nature was not to him

94
00:07:20,108 --> 00:07:23,921
that treasury of delight it was to his sisters.

95
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:29,940
He expressed once and but once in my hearing, a strong sense of the rugged

96
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:33,461
charm of the hills, and an inborn affection for

97
00:07:33,463 --> 00:07:37,360
the dark roof and horny walls, he called his home.

98
00:07:38,279 --> 00:07:44,019
But there was more of gloom than pleasure in the tone and words in which the

99
00:07:44,021 --> 00:07:47,749
sentiment was manifested, and never did he seem to

100
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:51,239
roam the moors for the sake of their soothing silence.

101
00:07:52,279 --> 00:07:57,040
Never seek out or dwell upon the thousand peaceful delights they could yield.

102
00:07:57,879 --> 00:08:01,792
In communicative as he was, some time elapsed

103
00:08:01,792 --> 00:08:05,260
before I had an opportunity of gauging his mind.

104
00:08:05,879 --> 00:08:08,550
I first got an idea of its caliber when I

105
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:12,341
heard him preach in his own church at Morton.

106
00:08:12,959 --> 00:08:17,339
I wish I could describe that sermon, but it is past my power.

107
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:21,980
I cannot even render faithfully the effect it produced on me.

108
00:08:22,739 --> 00:08:27,800
It began calm, and indeed, as far as delivery and pitcher voice went,

109
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:29,599
it was calm to the end.

110
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:34,517
An earnestly felt, yet strictly restrained zeal breathed soon

111
00:08:34,519 --> 00:08:38,680
in the distinct accents and prompted the nervous language.

112
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:43,819
This grew to force, compressed, condensed, controlled.

113
00:08:44,699 --> 00:08:49,300
The heart was thrilled, and the mind astonished by the power of the preacher,

114
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,139
neither was softened.

115
00:08:51,879 --> 00:08:56,519
Throughout, there was a strange bitterness, an absence of consolatory

116
00:08:56,521 --> 00:09:03,099
gentleness, stern illusions to Calvinistic doctrines, election predestination,

117
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,120
reprobation, were frequent.

118
00:09:06,019 --> 00:09:10,980
And each reference to these points sounded like a sentence pronounced for doom.

119
00:09:11,839 --> 00:09:17,980
When he had done, instead of feeling better, calmer, more enlightened by his

120
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:22,319
discourse, I experienced an inexpressible sadness.

121
00:09:23,279 --> 00:09:29,160
For it seemed to me, I know not whether equally so to others, that the eloquence

122
00:09:29,161 --> 00:09:34,900
to which I had been listening had sprung from a depth where lay turbid of

123
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:39,300
disappointment, where moved troubling impulses of

124
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:42,739
insatiate yearnings and disquieting aspirations.

125
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:49,900
I was sure, Syngen Rivers, pure lived conscientious zealous as he was,

126
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:54,760
had not yet found that piece of God, which passeth all understanding.

127
00:09:55,519 --> 00:10:00,400
He had no more found it, I thought, than had I, with my concealed and wracking

128
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:03,300
regrets for my broken idol and lost elicium.

129
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:08,158
Regrets to which I have latterly avoided referring, but

130
00:10:08,158 --> 00:10:11,540
which possessed me and tyrannized over me ruthlessly.

131
00:10:12,699 --> 00:10:14,760
Meantime, a month was gone.

132
00:10:16,099 --> 00:10:19,783
Diana and Mary were soon to leave more house and return

133
00:10:19,783 --> 00:10:22,980
to the far different life and scene which awaited them.

134
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:30,400
As governesses in a large, fashionable south of England city, where each held a

135
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:36,940
situation in families by whose wealthy and haughty members, they were regarded only

136
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:43,040
as humble dependents, and who neither knew nor sought out their innate excellences,

137
00:10:43,839 --> 00:10:48,319
and appreciated only their acquired accomplishments as they appreciated the

138
00:10:48,321 --> 00:10:52,220
skill of their cook, or the taste of their waiting-woman.

139
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:58,660
Mr. Syngen had said nothing to me yet about the employment he had promised to

140
00:10:58,661 --> 00:11:05,199
obtain for me, yet it became urgent that I should have a vocation of some kind.

141
00:11:05,959 --> 00:11:12,760
One morning, being left alone with him a few minutes in the parlour, I ventured to

142
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:19,120
approach the window recess which is table chair and desk consecrated as a kind of

143
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:25,099
study, and I was going to speak, though not very well knowing in what words

144
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:30,160
to frame my inquiry, for it is at all times difficult to break the ice of

145
00:11:30,161 --> 00:11:34,980
reserve, glassing over such natures as his, when he saved me the trouble,

146
00:11:35,599 --> 00:11:40,059
by being the first to commence a dialogue, looking up as I drew near.

147
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:44,500
You have a question to ask of me, he said.

148
00:11:46,239 --> 00:11:49,260
Yes, I wish to know whether you have heard of

149
00:11:49,262 --> 00:11:52,661
any service I can offer myself to undertake.

150
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:59,680
I found or devised something for you three weeks ago, but as you seemed both useful

151
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:04,779
and happy here, as my sisters had evidently become attached to you,

152
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:11,339
and your society gave them unusual pleasure, I deemed it inexperient to break

153
00:12:11,341 --> 00:12:13,913
in on your mutual comfort till their approaching

154
00:12:13,915 --> 00:12:17,080
departure from marsh end should render yours necessary.

155
00:12:18,599 --> 00:12:25,000
And they will go in three days now, I said, yes, and when they go,

156
00:12:25,559 --> 00:12:28,059
I shall return to the parsinage at Morton.

157
00:12:28,919 --> 00:12:33,239
Hanna will accompany me, and this old house will be shut up.

158
00:12:34,279 --> 00:12:39,940
I waited a few moments, expecting he would go on with the subject first broached,

159
00:12:40,699 --> 00:12:43,720
but he seemed to have entered another train of reflection.

160
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:48,739
His look denoted abstraction from me and my business.

161
00:12:49,459 --> 00:12:53,385
I was obliged to recall him to a theme which was of

162
00:12:53,385 --> 00:12:56,459
necessity one of close and anxious interest to me.

163
00:12:57,739 --> 00:13:00,419
What is the employment you had in view, Mr. Rivers?

164
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,620
I hope this delay will not have increased the difficulty of securing it.

165
00:13:05,379 --> 00:13:09,521
Oh, no, since it is an employment which depends only

166
00:13:09,521 --> 00:13:14,360
on me to give and you to accept, he again paused.

167
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,440
There seemed a reluctance to continue.

168
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:24,519
I grew impatient, a restless movement or two, and an eager and exacting glance

169
00:13:24,521 --> 00:13:28,260
fastened on his face, conveyed the feeling to him as

170
00:13:28,262 --> 00:13:33,139
effectively as words could have done, and with less trouble.

171
00:13:34,599 --> 00:13:37,500
You need be in no hurry to hear, he said.

172
00:13:38,459 --> 00:13:42,760
Let me frankly tell you I have nothing eligible or profitable to suggest.

173
00:13:43,599 --> 00:13:50,500
Before I explain, recall if you please my notice clearly given that if I helped you,

174
00:13:51,099 --> 00:13:54,080
it must be as the blind man would help the lame.

175
00:13:55,000 --> 00:14:01,760
I am poor, for I find that when I have paid my father's debts, all the patrimony

176
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:07,360
remaining to me will be this crumbling range, the row of scatheed furs behind,

177
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:12,559
and the patch of morish soil with the u -trees and hollybushes in front.

178
00:14:13,699 --> 00:14:20,040
I am obscure, Rivers is an old name, but of the three sole descendants of the

179
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:25,680
race, two earn the dependence crossed among strangers, and the third considers

180
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:30,500
himself an alien from his native country, not only for life, but in death.

181
00:14:31,199 --> 00:14:38,540
Yes, and deems, and is bound to deem, himself honoured by the lot, and aspires,

182
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:44,519
but after the day, when the cross of separation from fleshly ties shall be laid

183
00:14:44,521 --> 00:14:49,279
on his shoulders, and when the head of that church militant of whose humblest

184
00:14:49,281 --> 00:14:55,220
members he is one shall give the word, rise, follow me.

185
00:14:56,839 --> 00:15:02,339
Sinjin said these words, as he pronounced his sermons, with a quiet, deep voice,

186
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:08,879
with an unflushed cheek, and a co -rascating radiance of glance, he resumed.

187
00:15:09,099 --> 00:15:12,273
And since I am myself poor and obscure, I can

188
00:15:12,273 --> 00:15:16,580
offer you but a service of poverty and obscurity.

189
00:15:17,459 --> 00:15:21,540
You may even think it degrading, for I see now your habits have been what

190
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:27,800
the world calls refined, your tastes leaned to the ideal, and your society has

191
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:31,858
at least been amongst the educated, but I consider

192
00:15:31,858 --> 00:15:35,639
that no service degrades which can better our race.

193
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:42,819
I hold that the more arid and unreclaimed the soil where the Christian laborers'

194
00:15:42,919 --> 00:15:47,599
task of tillage is appointed him, the scantier the mead his toil brings,

195
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,639
the higher the honour.

196
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:54,860
His, under such circumstances, is the destiny of the pioneer,

197
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:58,059
and the first pioneers of the gospel were the apostles.

198
00:15:58,779 --> 00:16:01,900
Their captain was Jesus, the Redeemer, himself.

199
00:16:03,199 --> 00:16:07,959
Well, I said, as he again paused, proceed.

200
00:16:09,059 --> 00:16:11,180
He looked at me before he proceeded.

201
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:15,358
Indeed, he seemed leisurely to read my face, as if

202
00:16:15,358 --> 00:16:18,720
its features and lines were characters on a page.

203
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:22,635
The conclusions drawn from this scrutiny, he

204
00:16:22,637 --> 00:16:26,300
partially expressed in his succeeding observations.

205
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:33,819
I believe you will accept the post I offer you, said he, and hold it for a while.

206
00:16:34,839 --> 00:16:36,459
Not permanently, though.

207
00:16:37,239 --> 00:16:42,680
Any more than I could permanently keep the narrow and narrowing, the tranquil,

208
00:16:42,959 --> 00:16:48,019
hidden office of English country incumbent, for in your nature is an alloy,

209
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:53,160
as detrimental to repose as that in mine, though of a different kind.

210
00:16:54,099 --> 00:16:58,239
Do explain, I urged, when he halted once more.

211
00:16:59,019 --> 00:17:00,019
I will.

212
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:05,400
And you shall hear how poor the proposal is, how trivial, how cramping,

213
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,167
I shall not stay long at Morton, now that my

214
00:17:09,167 --> 00:17:12,339
father is dead, and that I am my own master.

215
00:17:13,879 --> 00:17:19,160
I shall leave the place, probably in the course of a 12-month, but while I do stay,

216
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:22,580
I will exert myself to the utmost for its improvement.

217
00:17:23,879 --> 00:17:28,379
Morton, when I came to it two years ago, had no school.

218
00:17:29,599 --> 00:17:33,459
The children of the poor were excluded from every hope of progress.

219
00:17:34,099 --> 00:17:36,199
I established one for boys.

220
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:39,680
I mean now to open a second school for girls.

221
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:44,565
I have hired a building for the purpose, with a cottage

222
00:17:44,567 --> 00:17:48,239
of two rooms attached to it, for the mistress's house.

223
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:51,220
Her salary will be 30 pounds a year.

224
00:17:52,239 --> 00:17:56,148
Her house is already furnished, very simply, but

225
00:17:56,148 --> 00:17:59,440
sufficiently by the kindness of a lady, Miss Oliver.

226
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:06,599
The only daughter of the sole rich man in my parish, Mr. Oliver, the proprietor of a

227
00:18:06,601 --> 00:18:09,019
needle factory and iron foundry in the valley.

228
00:18:09,959 --> 00:18:15,000
The same lady pays for the education and clothing of an orphan from the workhouse.

229
00:18:15,839 --> 00:18:20,260
On condition that she shall aid the mistress in such menial offices connected

230
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:24,016
with her own house and the school, as her occupation of

231
00:18:24,017 --> 00:18:29,180
teaching will prevent her having time to discharge in person.

232
00:18:29,919 --> 00:18:32,279
Will you be this mistress?

233
00:18:33,639 --> 00:18:36,180
He put the question rather hurriedly.

234
00:18:37,139 --> 00:18:44,620
He seemed half to expect an indignant or at least a disdainful rejection of the offer.

235
00:18:45,559 --> 00:18:49,807
Not knowing all my thoughts and feelings, though guessing some,

236
00:18:49,807 --> 00:18:52,959
he could not tell in what light the lot would appear to me.

237
00:18:53,839 --> 00:18:59,500
In truth, it was humble, but then it was sheltered, and I wanted a safe asylum.

238
00:19:00,099 --> 00:19:01,099
It was plotting.

239
00:19:01,639 --> 00:19:06,760
But then, compared with that of a governess in a rich house, it was independent.

240
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:11,639
And the fear of servitude with strangers entered my soul like iron.

241
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:16,279
It was not ignoble, not unworthy, not mentally degrading.

242
00:19:16,819 --> 00:19:18,099
I made my decision.

243
00:19:19,599 --> 00:19:24,849
I thank you for the proposal, Mr. Rivers, and I accept it with all my heart.

244
00:19:25,970 --> 00:19:28,190
But you comprehend me, he said.

245
00:19:29,230 --> 00:19:30,230
It is a village school.

246
00:19:30,809 --> 00:19:34,930
Your scholars will be only poor girls, cottages, children at the best,

247
00:19:35,209 --> 00:19:36,209
farmers, daughters.

248
00:19:36,949 --> 00:19:42,690
Knitting, sowing, reading, writing, ciphering will be all you will have to teach.

249
00:19:42,970 --> 00:19:45,069
What will you do with your accomplishments?

250
00:19:46,110 --> 00:19:46,430
What?

251
00:19:46,910 --> 00:19:50,169
With the largest portion of your mind, sentiments, tastes.

252
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:53,110
Save them till they are wanted.

253
00:19:53,809 --> 00:19:54,809
They will keep.

254
00:19:55,629 --> 00:19:57,370
You know what you undertake then.

255
00:19:58,209 --> 00:20:01,934
I do, he now smiled, and not a bitter or a sad

256
00:20:01,934 --> 00:20:06,110
smile, but one well pleased and deeply gratified.

257
00:20:06,389 --> 00:20:08,949
And when will you commence the exercise of your function?

258
00:20:09,989 --> 00:20:13,709
I will go to my house tomorrow and open the school if you like next week.

259
00:20:14,669 --> 00:20:16,389
Very well, so be it.

260
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:20,190
He rose and walked through the room.

261
00:20:20,910 --> 00:20:23,069
Standing still, he again looked at me.

262
00:20:23,709 --> 00:20:24,709
He shook his head.

263
00:20:25,989 --> 00:20:28,050
What do you disapprove of, Mr. Rivers?

264
00:20:28,650 --> 00:20:29,650
I asked.

265
00:20:29,989 --> 00:20:31,790
You will not stay at Morton Long.

266
00:20:32,269 --> 00:20:33,269
No, no.

267
00:20:33,610 --> 00:20:34,610
Why?

268
00:20:34,750 --> 00:20:36,669
What is your reason for saying so?

269
00:20:37,730 --> 00:20:39,269
I read it in your eye.

270
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:42,095
It is not of that description which promises

271
00:20:42,097 --> 00:20:45,031
the maintenance of an even tenor in life.

272
00:20:45,550 --> 00:20:47,110
I am not ambitious.

273
00:20:48,010 --> 00:20:49,889
He started at the word ambitious.

274
00:20:50,569 --> 00:20:52,550
He repeated, no.

275
00:20:53,349 --> 00:20:54,910
What made you think of ambition?

276
00:20:55,730 --> 00:20:56,730
Who is ambitious?

277
00:20:56,849 --> 00:20:57,849
I know I am.

278
00:20:58,349 --> 00:20:59,750
But how did you find it out?

279
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:02,349
I was speaking of myself.

280
00:21:03,169 --> 00:21:06,069
Well, if you are not ambitious, you are, he paused.

281
00:21:06,550 --> 00:21:07,550
What?

282
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:10,510
I was going to say impassioned.

283
00:21:11,250 --> 00:21:15,410
But perhaps you would have misunderstood the word and been displeased.

284
00:21:16,029 --> 00:21:22,071
I mean, that human affections and sympathies have a most powerful hold on you.

285
00:21:22,430 --> 00:21:26,589
I am sure you cannot long be content to pass your leisure in solitude,

286
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:32,150
and to devote your working hours to a monotonous labour wholly void of stimulus.

287
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:36,750
Any more than I can be content, he added with emphasis.

288
00:21:37,430 --> 00:21:42,389
To live here buried in morass, pent in with mountains, my nature that God

289
00:21:42,391 --> 00:21:48,290
gave me contravened, my faculties, heaven bestowed, paralysed, made useless.

290
00:21:49,110 --> 00:21:51,750
You hear now how I contradict myself.

291
00:21:52,569 --> 00:21:58,269
I, who preached contentment with a humble lot, and justified the vocation even of

292
00:21:58,271 --> 00:22:03,989
hewers of wood and drawers of water in God's service, I, his ordained minister,

293
00:22:04,589 --> 00:22:06,389
almost rave in my restlessness.

294
00:22:07,110 --> 00:22:12,290
Well, propensities and principles must be reconciled by some means.

295
00:22:12,970 --> 00:22:13,970
He left the room.

296
00:22:15,529 --> 00:22:20,250
In this brief hour, I had learnt more of him than in the whole previous month,

297
00:22:21,069 --> 00:22:22,470
yet still he puzzled me.

298
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:27,404
Diana and Mary Rivers became more sad and silent as the

299
00:22:27,406 --> 00:22:30,769
day approached for leaving their brother and their home.

300
00:22:31,690 --> 00:22:36,569
They both tried to appear as usual, but the sorrow they had to struggle

301
00:22:36,571 --> 00:22:41,550
against was one that could not be entirely conquered or concealed.

302
00:22:43,209 --> 00:22:46,158
Diana intimated that this would be a different

303
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:49,271
parting from any they had ever yet known.

304
00:22:49,949 --> 00:22:50,949
It would probably,

305
00:22:57,330 --> 00:23:03,589
as far he will sacrifice all to his long framed resolves, she said.

306
00:23:04,489 --> 00:23:07,150
Natural affection and feelings more potent still.

307
00:23:07,910 --> 00:23:12,110
Sinjin looks quiet, Jane, but he hides a fever in his vitals.

308
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:18,069
You would think him gentle, yet in some things he is inexorable as death.

309
00:23:18,809 --> 00:23:21,474
And the worst of it is, my conscience will hardly

310
00:23:21,476 --> 00:23:24,391
permit me to dissuade him from his severe decision.

311
00:23:24,730 --> 00:23:27,250
Certainly I cannot for a moment blame him for it.

312
00:23:27,750 --> 00:23:32,489
It is right, noble, Christian, yet it breaks my heart.

313
00:23:33,290 --> 00:23:36,190
And the tears gushed to her fine eyes.

314
00:23:37,430 --> 00:23:39,730
Mary bent her head low over her work.

315
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:42,330
We are now without father.

316
00:23:43,150 --> 00:23:45,169
We shall soon be without home and brother.

317
00:23:46,150 --> 00:23:47,150
She murmured.

318
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:52,769
At that moment, a little accident supervened, which seemed decreed by fate

319
00:23:52,771 --> 00:23:57,989
purposely to prove the truth of the adage that misfortunes never come singly,

320
00:23:58,709 --> 00:24:00,764
and to add to their distress is the vexing

321
00:24:00,766 --> 00:24:04,311
one of the slip between the cup and the lip.

322
00:24:04,989 --> 00:24:06,930
Sinjin passed the window reading a letter.

323
00:24:07,709 --> 00:24:08,709
He entered.

324
00:24:09,910 --> 00:24:12,290
Our uncle John is dead, said he.

325
00:24:13,470 --> 00:24:16,790
Both the sisters seemed struck, not shocked or appalled.

326
00:24:17,489 --> 00:24:20,550
The tidings appeared in their eyes rather momentous than afflicting.

327
00:24:21,809 --> 00:24:22,809
Dead?

328
00:24:23,190 --> 00:24:24,190
repeated Diana.

329
00:24:24,589 --> 00:24:28,069
Yes, she riveted a searching gaze on her brother's face.

330
00:24:29,029 --> 00:24:32,309
And what then she demanded in a low voice?

331
00:24:33,269 --> 00:24:37,290
What then died he replied, maintaining a marble immobility of feature?

332
00:24:38,309 --> 00:24:39,309
What then?

333
00:24:39,669 --> 00:24:40,669
Why nothing?

334
00:24:41,349 --> 00:24:42,349
Read.

335
00:24:42,430 --> 00:24:44,290
He threw the letter into her lap.

336
00:24:44,930 --> 00:24:47,209
She glanced over it and handed it to Mary.

337
00:24:48,010 --> 00:24:54,410
Mary perused it in silence and returned it to her brother All three looked at each

338
00:24:54,411 --> 00:25:00,230
other and all three smiled, a dreary, pensive smile enough.

339
00:25:01,690 --> 00:25:06,790
Our men, we can yet live, said Diana at last.

340
00:25:08,209 --> 00:25:13,709
At any rate, it makes us no worse off than we were before remarked Mary.

341
00:25:15,150 --> 00:25:20,290
Only it forces rather strongly on the mind the picture of what might have been,

342
00:25:20,930 --> 00:25:26,050
said Mr. Rivers, and contrasts it somewhat too vividly with what is.

343
00:25:27,050 --> 00:25:30,589
He folded the letter, locked it in his desk and again went out.

344
00:25:31,889 --> 00:25:33,569
For some minutes no one spoke.

345
00:25:34,569 --> 00:25:35,830
Diana then turned to me.

346
00:25:37,010 --> 00:25:41,110
Jane, you will wander at us in our mysteries, she said.

347
00:25:42,089 --> 00:25:44,839
And think us hard-hearted beings, not to be more

348
00:25:44,841 --> 00:25:48,230
moved at the death of so near a relation as an uncle.

349
00:25:49,190 --> 00:25:51,930
But we have never seen him or known him.

350
00:25:52,569 --> 00:25:56,569
He was my mother's brother, my father and he quarreled long ago.

351
00:25:57,669 --> 00:26:00,661
It was by his advice that my father risked most of

352
00:26:00,663 --> 00:26:04,010
his property in the speculation that ruined him.

353
00:26:05,129 --> 00:26:07,650
Mutual recrimination passed between them.

354
00:26:08,410 --> 00:26:11,529
They parted in anger and were never reconciled.

355
00:26:12,589 --> 00:26:16,489
My uncle engaged afterwards in more prosperous undertakings.

356
00:26:16,830 --> 00:26:21,010
It appears he realized a fortune of 20,000 pounds.

357
00:26:21,750 --> 00:26:25,529
He was never married and had no near kindred but ourselves

358
00:26:25,531 --> 00:26:29,309
and one other person, not more closely related than we.

359
00:26:30,510 --> 00:26:33,821
My father always cherished the idea that he would

360
00:26:33,822 --> 00:26:37,250
atone for his error by leaving his possessions to us.

361
00:26:38,589 --> 00:26:43,489
That letter informs us that he has bequeathed every penny to the other

362
00:26:43,491 --> 00:26:50,589
relation, with the exception of 30 guineas to be divided between Sinjin, Diana and

363
00:26:50,591 --> 00:26:54,250
Mary Rivers, for the purchase of three morning rings.

364
00:26:55,110 --> 00:26:57,669
He had a right, of course, to do as he pleased.

365
00:26:58,569 --> 00:27:03,889
And yet a momentary damp is cast on the spirits by the receipt of such news.

366
00:27:04,989 --> 00:27:10,330
Mary and I would have esteemed ourselves rich with a thousand pounds each,

367
00:27:11,050 --> 00:27:14,476
and to Sinjin such as some would have been valuable,

368
00:27:14,476 --> 00:27:17,190
for the good it would have enabled him to do.

369
00:27:18,150 --> 00:27:22,436
This explanation given, the subject was dropped, and no further

370
00:27:22,436 --> 00:27:27,190
reference made to it by either Mr. Rivers or his sisters.

371
00:27:28,430 --> 00:27:32,766
The next day I left Marsh End for Morton, the day

372
00:27:32,767 --> 00:27:37,169
after, Diana and Mary quitted it for distant B.

373
00:27:38,750 --> 00:27:43,146
In a week, Mr. Rivers and Hannah repaired to the

374
00:27:43,148 --> 00:27:46,930
Parsonage, and so the old Grange was abandoned.
